An exhaustive search of official UNESCO records, affiliated bodies, and related academic sources found no evidence of any declaration by UNESCO designating the Nadar community as the world's most ancient race. More significantly, UNESCO's own authoritative historical position, formalized in its [1950 Statement on Race](http://www.honestthinking.org/en/unesco/UNESCO.1950.Statement_on_Race.htm), explicitly refutes the scientific basis for ranking human groups by antiquity, stating that racial classifications are not static or hierarchical and that all humans belong to the same species.